.TH TUXDIRSTAT 1 "2026-11-06" "TuxDirStat 1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tuxdirstat, tuxdirstat-gtk3, tuxdirstat-gtk4, tuxdirstat-tk \- disk usage analyzer with tree, extension list and treemap
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuxdirstat
.RI [ folder | snapshot.json ]
.br
.B tuxdirstat
.I output-options
.RI [ other-options ]
.I folder
.br
.B tuxdirstat
.I output-options
.B \-\-import
.I snapshot.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TuxDirStat
scans a folder and shows how its space is used: a tree sorted by size, a list of file
extensions and a shaded treemap where every file is a box whose area matches its size.
.B tuxdirstat
is the Qt interface;
.BR tuxdirstat-gtk3 ,
.B tuxdirstat-gtk4
and
.B tuxdirstat-tk
are the same program with other toolkits. All of them share the command line options below.
.PP
Without an output option a window opens. Giving a folder scans it right away; giving a
snapshot file opens it instead.
.PP
The window also offers duplicate file search, cleanup suggestions, search, snapshot
comparison, usage by owner, CSV export, age coloring, an administrator (read-only) scan
through
.BR pkexec (1)
and, on Arch Linux, package ownership checks.
.SH OUTPUT OPTIONS
These print results (or write files) and exit without opening a window. They can be
combined; each runs in the order given.
.TP
.B \-\-report
Text report: the largest folders, files and extensions.
.TP
.BI \-\-find " query"
Search the scan. Words match file names (\fB*\fR and \fB?\fR are wildcards). Filters:
\fB>100M\fR, \fB<1G\fR (size), \fBolder:1y\fR, \fBnewer:2w\fR (last change; units h, d, w, m, y),
\fBtype:f\fR or \fBtype:d\fR, \fBext:mp4,mkv\fR, \fBuser:\fIname\fR and \fBpath:\fItext\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-duplicates
List files with identical contents. Sizes are compared first, then the first 64 KB and then
the whole file. Hard links to the same data are not reported.
.TP
.B \-\-cleanup
Caches, build output (node_modules, CMake and Cargo build folders, Python caches), trash,
unfinished downloads, the pacman cache, the systemd journal, crash dumps and unused
Docker, Podman or Flatpak data.
.TP
.B \-\-owners
Disk usage per file owner.
.TP
.B \-\-unowned
Arch Linux: files and folders under /usr, /etc and /opt that no pacman package owns.
Scan / (or one of those folders) for this.
.TP
.BI \-\-export " file"
Save the scan as a snapshot in the ncdu JSON export format.
.TP
.BI \-\-csv " file"
Write every file and folder to a CSV file.
.TP
.BI \-\-compare " snapshot"
Show what grew, shrank, appeared or disappeared since an earlier snapshot.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-import " file"
Read a snapshot (written by TuxDirStat or by \fBncdu \-o\fR) instead of scanning.
Files ending in .gz, .zst, .xz or .bz2 are decompressed first.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " n"
Rows per list in \fB\-\-report\fR (default 15).
.TP
.B \-\-apparent
Use the apparent file size instead of the space used on disk.
.TP
.B \-\-group
Group many similar items (such as game assets) in \fB\-\-report\fR and list the most crowded groups.
.TP
.BI \-\-group\-min " n"
Minimum number of items per group (default 16).
.TP
.B \-\-all\-fs
Cross into other file systems. By default the scan stays on the starting file system
(btrfs subvolumes of the same device are included) and always skips virtual file systems.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " en|tr"
Interface language. The default follows the saved setting, then the locale.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tuxdirstat/settings.conf
Settings shared by all interfaces: size mode, grouping, theme, language, age coloring.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tuxdirstat ~/Games
tuxdirstat \-\-report \-\-top 20 /var
tuxdirstat \-\-find '*.iso >1G older:1y' ~
tuxdirstat \-\-export home\-$(date +%F).json ~
tuxdirstat \-\-compare home\-2026\-10\-01.json ~
sudo tuxdirstat \-\-unowned /
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if a scan, file or tool failed, 2 for wrong usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR du (1),
.BR ncdu (1),
.BR pacman (8)
